# Akev development settings. Copy this file to .env (git ignores it) and uncomment what you need.
#
# Read by every `make` target, scripts/release.sh, and `scripts/with-env <command>` for cargo or
# bun commands you run yourself. The VITE_ lines are read by the UI dev server only, so they never
# end up in a build. A variable already set in your shell wins over this file.
#
# Format: KEY=value, one per line. Quotes and $HOME work; ~ doesn't.
# Official releases are built by CI and never see this file. Keep production secrets out of it:
# scripts/release.sh reads those from the file AKEV_LICENSING_ENV names.

# --- The Akev you run: make daemon, make dev, cargo run -p akev-cli ------------------------------
# A separate data folder (CA, settings, rules, saved traffic), so development never touches your
# real one or collides with a running desktop app. The CLI only: the desktop app always uses the
# standard folder.
# AKEV_DATA_DIR=$HOME/.akev-dev
# A fixed API token (24+ characters, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 24`), so the UI stays signed in when
# you restart the daemon.
# AKEV_TOKEN=
# A Pro license key for these runs (not stored).
# AKEV_LICENSE=
# The daemon that CLI commands such as `akev tail` talk to (default: found via the data folder).
# AKEV_URL=http://127.0.0.1:45456
# Logging: akev=debug, akev_proxy=trace, …
# RUST_LOG=akev=debug
# Write TLS session keys here, so Wireshark can decrypt Akev's upstream connections.
# SSLKEYLOGFILE=$HOME/akev-tls-keys.log
# Check for updates against another manifest (for example a test release's latest.json).
# AKEV_UPDATE_MANIFEST_URL=

# --- The UI dev server: make ui-dev, make dev ----------------------------------------------------
# Talk to this daemon directly instead of through the dev server's /api proxy.
# VITE_AKEV_URL=http://127.0.0.1:45456
# Always run on the built-in mock backend (demo traffic, no daemon). `?mock` in the URL does it
# for one tab.
# VITE_MOCK=1

# --- Builds ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Also trust these license public keys (comma-separated), so keys you sign yourself activate.
# Changing it rebuilds akev-api. Never set it in a build you give to anyone. This one is the test
# key from crates/akev-api/tests/common/pro.rs; with AKEV_E2E_TEST_LICENSE=1 (below), `make e2e`
# also runs the valid-license test.
# AKEV_LICENSE_PUBLIC_KEY=A6EHv_POEL4dcN0Y50vAmWfk1jCbpQ1fHdyGZBJVMbg
# This build's release date (YYYY-MM-DD). A license covers versions released up to its
# updates-until date, so a later date shows how an expired license behaves.
# AKEV_RELEASE_DATE=2028-01-01
# Let a release build embed a placeholder page when ui/dist has no built UI.
# AKEV_ALLOW_PLACEHOLDER_UI=1
# Fail the build when no JDK is found, instead of leaving out the JVM agent (CI and releases do).
# AKEV_AGENT_REQUIRE_JDK=1
# The JDK that builds the JVM agent (default: javac on PATH).
# JAVA_HOME=

# --- Tests ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run the valid-license end-to-end test (needs AKEV_LICENSE_PUBLIC_KEY above).
# AKEV_E2E_TEST_LICENSE=1
# Run one Playwright project: daemon or visual. Usually for one run: AKEV_E2E_PROJECT=daemon make e2e
# AKEV_E2E_PROJECT=daemon
# Rewrite the code-generation golden files instead of comparing with them (one run only).
# AKEV_UPDATE_GOLDEN=1
# More iterations, or another seed, for the content decoders' robustness test.
# AKEV_FUZZ_ITERS=100000
# AKEV_FUZZ_SEED=1
# The Chrome or Chromium binary for UI screenshots (ui/scripts/shot.ts).
# CHROME=/usr/bin/chromium-browser

# --- Releasing: scripts/release.sh ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The website checkout, whose licensing CLI lists refunded and charged-back licenses.
# AKEV_WEBSITE_DIR=../akev-website
# The env file with the live Stripe settings (STRIPE_SECRET_KEY, STRIPE_PAYMENT_LINKS). Keep it
# outside the repository.
# AKEV_LICENSING_ENV=$HOME/.config/akev/production.env
# Release without refreshing the revocation list.
# AKEV_SKIP_REVOCATION=1
